From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Spencer <hspencer@rv1106g3>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] rga2: fix get_user_pages_remote for Linux 6.6

Linux 6.6 changed get_user_pages_remote() to take six arguments.
The Rockchip RGA2 driver still passes the obsolete seventh argument.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Harry Spencer <hspencer@rv1106g3>

---
 drivers/video/rockchip/rga2/rga2_mmu_info.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga2/rga2_mmu_info.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga2/rga2_mmu_info.c
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/rga2/rga2_mmu_info.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/rga2/rga2_mmu_info.c
@@ -938,7 +938,7 @@ static int rga2_MapUserMemory(struct rga2_mem_info_t *mem_info)
 #else
 	result = get_user_pages_remote(current->mm, Memory << PAGE_SHIFT,
-				       pageCount, writeFlag, pages, NULL, NULL);
+				       pageCount, writeFlag, pages, NULL);
 #endif